  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "01_method",
      "title": "What a test can show",
      "audio": "english/audio/01_method.mp3",
      "duration_seconds": 88.089274,
      "clip_end_seconds": 27.9325,
      "duration_in_frames": 2643,
      "clip_end_frame": 838,
      "from_frame": 0,
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "A green test suite is not enough to",
          "startMs": 0,
          "endMs": 1442,
          "timestampMs": 0,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "claim that a model works.",
          "startMs": 1500,
          "endMs": 2738,
          "timestampMs": 1500,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "This study evaluates a QA instrument, not a",
          "startMs": 3163,
          "endMs": 5447,
          "timestampMs": 3163,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "new theory.",
          "startMs": 5505,
          "endMs": 6028,
          "timestampMs": 5505,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Before testing, we fix the domain, units, tolerance,",
          "startMs": 6531,
          "endMs": 10023,
          "timestampMs": 6531,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "invariants, and an independent oracle.",
          "startMs": 10149,
          "endMs": 12490,
          "timestampMs": 10149,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Then we run a baseline and specific mutations,",
          "startMs": 12993,
          "endMs": 15035,
          "timestampMs": 12993,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "such as reversing a sign or doubling a",
          "startMs": 15209,
          "endMs": 17318,
          "timestampMs": 15209,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "coefficient.",
          "startMs": 17396,
          "endMs": 18063,
          "timestampMs": 17396,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The question is whether tests detect deliberate changes.",
          "startMs": 18431,
          "endMs": 20753,
          "timestampMs": 18431,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Each result stays linked to its parameters, code,",
          "startMs": 21072,
          "endMs": 23559,
          "timestampMs": 21072,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and artifacts for later review.",
          "startMs": 23704,
          "endMs": 25155,
          "timestampMs": 23704,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "This separates model correctness from test sensitivity.",
          "startMs": 25581,
          "endMs": 27932,
          "timestampMs": 25581,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "If the program and oracle share a formula",
          "startMs": 28358,
          "endMs": 30196,
          "timestampMs": 28358,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and integrator, they can share an error.",
          "startMs": 30264,
          "endMs": 32576,
          "timestampMs": 30264,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "So the suite compares distinct implementations at multiple",
          "startMs": 32808,
          "endMs": 35469,
          "timestampMs": 32808,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "observations.",
          "startMs": 35508,
          "endMs": 36185,
          "timestampMs": 35508,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The contract defines success before results are known.",
          "startMs": 36552,
          "endMs": 38846,
          "timestampMs": 36552,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A failing baseline blocks interpretation of its mutants;",
          "startMs": 39165,
          "endMs": 41564,
          "timestampMs": 39165,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "a small variation may survive if it falls",
          "startMs": 41883,
          "endMs": 44022,
          "timestampMs": 41883,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "below tolerance.",
          "startMs": 44118,
          "endMs": 44960,
          "timestampMs": 44118,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The threshold is not changed afterward.",
          "startMs": 45386,
          "endMs": 46962,
          "timestampMs": 45386,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The package preserves hashes and outputs so reviewers",
          "startMs": 47466,
          "endMs": 49865,
          "timestampMs": 47466,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "can trace each classification.",
          "startMs": 49913,
          "endMs": 51288,
          "timestampMs": 49913,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "We distinguish synthetic calculations, kernel controls, and earlier",
          "startMs": 51790,
          "endMs": 55332,
          "timestampMs": 51790,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "campaigns.",
          "startMs": 55389,
          "endMs": 55999,
          "timestampMs": 55389,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "I’m Cristian Guerra, known as criguex, a Colombian",
          "startMs": 56579,
          "endMs": 59888,
          "timestampMs": 56579,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "QA Automation professional from Medellín, with more than",
          "startMs": 59947,
          "endMs": 62520,
          "timestampMs": 59947,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "eight years of experience.",
          "startMs": 62617,
          "endMs": 63758,
          "timestampMs": 62617,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "I authored this QA study and independent reproduction",
          "startMs": 64262,
          "endMs": 67077,
          "timestampMs": 64262,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "through contributions to strategy, mutations, resources, and validation.",
          "startMs": 67116,
          "endMs": 71489,
          "timestampMs": 67116,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "AI tools are disclosed as assistance for analysis",
          "startMs": 72166,
          "endMs": 74449,
          "timestampMs": 72166,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and code preparation, not as coauthors or co-discoverers.",
          "startMs": 74508,
          "endMs": 77526,
          "timestampMs": 74508,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "OpenAI is credited for the original proofs;",
          "startMs": 78029,
          "endMs": 80197,
          "timestampMs": 78029,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "this study does not claim authorship of them",
          "startMs": 80699,
          "endMs": 82392,
          "timestampMs": 80699,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "or discovery of a theorem.",
          "startMs": 82567,
          "endMs": 83786,
          "timestampMs": 82567,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The contribution is making tests, detected failures, and",
          "startMs": 84367,
          "endMs": 87114,
          "timestampMs": 84367,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "limits auditable.",
          "startMs": 87172,
          "endMs": 88082,
          "timestampMs": 87172,
          "confidence": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "02_models_rc",
      "title": "Nine synthetic models",
      "audio": "english/audio/02_models_rc.mp3",
      "duration_seconds": 101.475873,
      "clip_end_seconds": 36.222500000000004,
      "duration_in_frames": 3045,
      "clip_end_frame": 1087,
      "from_frame": 2643,
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "The suite contains nine synthetic models:",
          "startMs": 0,
          "endMs": 2080,
          "timestampMs": 0,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "an RC circuit, Newton cooling, second-order consumption, Beer–Lambert",
          "startMs": 2283,
          "endMs": 6869,
          "timestampMs": 2283,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "attenuation, Snell refraction, a thin lens, an acoustic",
          "startMs": 6918,
          "endMs": 10632,
          "timestampMs": 6918,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "interface, an illustrative Fechner scale, and a synthetic",
          "startMs": 10681,
          "endMs": 14009,
          "timestampMs": 10681,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "logistic response.",
          "startMs": 14068,
          "endMs": 15103,
          "timestampMs": 14068,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "One concrete example is the RC circuit.",
          "startMs": 15683,
          "endMs": 18043,
          "timestampMs": 15683,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "With one kiloohm and one millifarad, its nominal",
          "startMs": 18314,
          "endMs": 21120,
          "timestampMs": 18314,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "time constant is one second.",
          "startMs": 21159,
          "endMs": 22901,
          "timestampMs": 21159,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Deliberately changing tau changes the recorded output.",
          "startMs": 23403,
          "endMs": 26190,
          "timestampMs": 23403,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "These are reproducible calculations, not laboratory measurements.",
          "startMs": 26558,
          "endMs": 30098,
          "timestampMs": 26558,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Each model has three nondegenerate configurations in the",
          "startMs": 30466,
          "endMs": 33398,
          "timestampMs": 30466,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "fixed contract, with units and observations specified.",
          "startMs": 33446,
          "endMs": 36223,
          "timestampMs": 33446,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The RC case runs for three seconds, with",
          "startMs": 36900,
          "endMs": 39212,
          "timestampMs": 36900,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "sixty-four, one hundred twenty-eight, and two hundred fifty-six",
          "startMs": 39261,
          "endMs": 42831,
          "timestampMs": 39261,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "integration steps.",
          "startMs": 42898,
          "endMs": 43818,
          "timestampMs": 42898,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "At three seconds and the finest resolution, the",
          "startMs": 44137,
          "endMs": 46313,
          "timestampMs": 44137,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "baseline records 4.751 volts;",
          "startMs": 46372,
          "endMs": 48752,
          "timestampMs": 46372,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "doubling tau records 3.884.",
          "startMs": 49022,
          "endMs": 52370,
          "timestampMs": 49022,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "These are rounded JSON values, not physical readings.",
          "startMs": 52641,
          "endMs": 55118,
          "timestampMs": 52641,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The nominal time constant is resistance multiplied by",
          "startMs": 55428,
          "endMs": 57933,
          "timestampMs": 55428,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "capacitance:",
          "startMs": 58001,
          "endMs": 58784,
          "timestampMs": 58001,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "tau equals R times C.",
          "startMs": 58988,
          "endMs": 61319,
          "timestampMs": 58988,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Other oracles are distinct:",
          "startMs": 61745,
          "endMs": 63187,
          "timestampMs": 61745,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "closed-form solutions for several ODEs, bisection for Snell,",
          "startMs": 63390,
          "endMs": 67134,
          "timestampMs": 63390,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ray tracing for the lens, a boundary system",
          "startMs": 67453,
          "endMs": 69794,
          "timestampMs": 67453,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "for acoustics, and numerical integration for Fechner.",
          "startMs": 69852,
          "endMs": 73093,
          "timestampMs": 69852,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The logistic model is a synthetic response to",
          "startMs": 73597,
          "endMs": 75706,
          "timestampMs": 73597,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "normalized stimulus, between zero and one;",
          "startMs": 75773,
          "endMs": 78008,
          "timestampMs": 75773,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Fechner is illustrative, not a universal law.",
          "startMs": 78588,
          "endMs": 81694,
          "timestampMs": 78588,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Some configurations share mathematical structure after rescaling, so",
          "startMs": 81965,
          "endMs": 85797,
          "timestampMs": 81965,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "nine names do not mean nine independent regimes.",
          "startMs": 85864,
          "endMs": 88844,
          "timestampMs": 85864,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "No experimental measurements were used.",
          "startMs": 89425,
          "endMs": 91602,
          "timestampMs": 89425,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Plots retain units and calculated points.",
          "startMs": 92105,
          "endMs": 94311,
          "timestampMs": 92105,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The suite examines detection of known changes in",
          "startMs": 94813,
          "endMs": 97262,
          "timestampMs": 94813,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "controlled examples;",
          "startMs": 97329,
          "endMs": 98490,
          "timestampMs": 97329,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "it does not certify real-world performance.",
          "startMs": 98916,
          "endMs": 101470,
          "timestampMs": 98916,
          "confidence": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03_formal_controls",
      "title": "Narrow formal controls",
      "audio": "english/audio/03_formal_controls.mp3",
      "duration_seconds": 70.05839,
      "clip_end_seconds": 27.17666666666667,
      "duration_in_frames": 2102,
      "clip_end_frame": 816,
      "from_frame": 5688,
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "The kernel control uses a minimal fixture:",
          "startMs": 0,
          "endMs": 1935,
          "timestampMs": 0,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "target states zero equals zero and is proved",
          "startMs": 2138,
          "endMs": 4615,
          "timestampMs": 2138,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "with rfl.",
          "startMs": 4634,
          "endMs": 5398,
          "timestampMs": 4634,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The mutation keeps the declared type but replaces",
          "startMs": 5718,
          "endMs": 7827,
          "timestampMs": 5718,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "the proof value with a proof of True.",
          "startMs": 7856,
          "endMs": 9588,
          "timestampMs": 7856,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Lean and nanoda accept the baseline and reject",
          "startMs": 10013,
          "endMs": 11968,
          "timestampMs": 10013,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "that incompatible value.",
          "startMs": 11997,
          "endMs": 13052,
          "timestampMs": 11997,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "This is a typechecking control for one declaration,",
          "startMs": 13371,
          "endMs": 15567,
          "timestampMs": 13371,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "contrasting the declared type with the exported proof",
          "startMs": 15712,
          "endMs": 17802,
          "timestampMs": 15712,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "value.",
          "startMs": 17850,
          "endMs": 18238,
          "timestampMs": 17850,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Separately, Lean accepts a nonzero constant field in",
          "startMs": 18741,
          "endMs": 21159,
          "timestampMs": 18741,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "periodic Navier–Stokes, with zero pressure and force and",
          "startMs": 21218,
          "endMs": 23897,
          "timestampMs": 21218,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "unit viscosity.",
          "startMs": 23974,
          "endMs": 24826,
          "timestampMs": 23974,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "These controls have distinct scopes.",
          "startMs": 25407,
          "endMs": 27177,
          "timestampMs": 25407,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Lean reports that True does not match the",
          "startMs": 27322,
          "endMs": 28841,
          "timestampMs": 27322,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "expected type;",
          "startMs": 28880,
          "endMs": 29653,
          "timestampMs": 28880,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "nanoda reaches a definitional-equality assertion.",
          "startMs": 30022,
          "endMs": 32285,
          "timestampMs": 30022,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "This pair is a bounded control.",
          "startMs": 32604,
          "endMs": 34211,
          "timestampMs": 32604,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The periodic example is on a torus, and",
          "startMs": 34530,
          "endMs": 36281,
          "timestampMs": 34530,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "its axiom report lists three axioms:",
          "startMs": 36339,
          "endMs": 38119,
          "timestampMs": 36339,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.",
          "startMs": 38545,
          "endMs": 41128,
          "timestampMs": 38545,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A constant velocity does not have finite energy",
          "startMs": 41708,
          "endMs": 43624,
          "timestampMs": 41708,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "over all of R³, so it does not",
          "startMs": 43672,
          "endMs": 45375,
          "timestampMs": 43672,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "transfer to the Euclidean problem.",
          "startMs": 45395,
          "endMs": 46808,
          "timestampMs": 45395,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "After the clean-source build, Comparator independently rechecked the",
          "startMs": 47388,
          "endMs": 50136,
          "timestampMs": 47388,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Navier–Stokes and Euler challenges with both nanoda and",
          "startMs": 50184,
          "endMs": 53009,
          "timestampMs": 50184,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Lean.",
          "startMs": 53077,
          "endMs": 53435,
          "timestampMs": 53077,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Calibration included two positive fixtures accepted and four",
          "startMs": 53860,
          "endMs": 56579,
          "timestampMs": 53860,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "negative fixtures rejected before kernel calls.",
          "startMs": 56628,
          "endMs": 58891,
          "timestampMs": 56628,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "These recorded results are not universal verification.",
          "startMs": 59394,
          "endMs": 61968,
          "timestampMs": 59394,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Exact names appear on screen, and preserved artifacts",
          "startMs": 62335,
          "endMs": 64996,
          "timestampMs": 62335,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "let reviewers inspect the harness, declarations, and outputs",
          "startMs": 65063,
          "endMs": 68005,
          "timestampMs": 65063,
          "confidence": null
        },
        {
          "text": "without changing original theorem sources.",
          "startMs": 68043,
          "endMs": 70047,
          "timestampMs": 68043,
          "confidence": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
